Hypatia changes
===============

2.1 (not yet released)
----------------------

Results that differ from 2.0:

* The matrix4 rotations follow the right-hand rule, as their documentation
  says: matrix4_make_transformation_rotationf_x, _rotationf_y, _rotationf_z,
  _rotationq and matrix4_rotatev3.  In 2.0 they turned the other way.  A
  positive angle about an axis now turns counterclockwise when the axis
  points toward the viewer, the same as vector3_rotate_by_quaternion.
  matrix4_transformation_compose_EXP, which uses _rotationq, changes with
  them.  matrix4_set_from_euler_anglesf3_EXP and
  matrix4_make_transformation_rotationv3_EXP turn the other way too: they
  give Rz(z) * Ry(y) * Rx(x), the same rotation as
  quaternion_set_from_euler_anglesf3.
* vector3_rotate_by_quaternion was wrong for vectors not perpendicular to
  the axis (a sign in quaternion_multiplyv3).
* matrix4_multiplyv2 treats the vector as (x, y, 0, 1); 2.0 added the third
  column as if z were 1.
* matrix2/3/4_inverse return NULL only when the determinant is exactly zero
  (or NaN).  2.0 returned NULL when it was within HYP_EPSILON of zero, so a
  4x4 scale of 0.02 had no inverse.
* matrix2/3/4_invert return NULL, and leave the matrix unchanged, when it
  has no inverse.  2.0 returned the matrix in both cases, so the caller
  could not tell.
* vector2/3/4_normalize and quaternion_normalize leave only an exactly zero
  vector unchanged; 2.0 left anything shorter than HYP_EPSILON unchanged.
  Very long and very short vectors no longer overflow or underflow, and
  vector2_normalize no longer gives NaN.
* quaternion_inverse and quaternion_lerp have no shortcuts near 0 or 1, and
  quaternion_is_pure compares w relative to the length of the quaternion.
* quaternion_get_rotation_tov3 works for nearly opposite and opposite
  vectors (2.0 gave a near-zero or zero quaternion) and for vectors of any
  length.
* quaternion_get_axis_anglev3 works for a quaternion of any length (2.0
  gave NaN for one that was not unit length), and gives an angle in
  [0, pi] for q and -q alike.
* quaternion_get_euler_anglesf3 gives angles of the same rotation at and
  near gimbal lock (a pitch of +-pi/2), and for a quaternion of any length.

New functions:

* vector2/3/4_lerp, _clamp, _min, _max and _project; vector2/3_reflect;
  vector3_refract.
* matrix2/3/4_reciprocal_condition: how reliable an inverse is, 1 for a
  multiple of the identity and 0 for a matrix with no inverse.
* quaternion_set_from_matrix4: the unit quaternion of a rotation matrix
  (Shepperd's method).
* scalar_random_rangef: a random number in [min, max), evenly distributed.
* vector2/3/4_set_random_unit and quaternion_set_random_unit: evenly
  distributed directions and rotations.
* vector2_set_random_in_disk and vector3_set_random_in_ball: evenly
  distributed points.

New configuration macros:

* HYP_RANDOM() and HYP_RANDOM_MAX: the random number source of the random
  functions (default rand() and RAND_MAX).  Define both or neither.
* HYP_NO_RANDOM: leaves out the random functions, HYP_RANDOM,
  HYP_RANDOM_MAX, HYP_RANDOM_FLOAT and <stdlib.h>.

Deprecated:

* HYP_RANDOM_FLOAT: use scalar_random_rangef(-1, 1).  HYP_NO_DEPRECATED
  leaves it out.

Known problems in 2.1:

These experimental functions give wrong results; do not use them.

* matrix4_projection_perspective_fovy_rh_EXP, matrix4_projection_ortho3d_rh_EXP
  and matrix4_view_lookat_rh_EXP do not give correct projections.
* matrix4_multiplyv3_EXP is not the same as matrix4_multiplyv3; use
  matrix4_multiplyv3.
* matrix4_transformation_decompose_EXP always returns the identity rotation.
* quaternion_angle_between_EXP and quaternion_difference_EXP treat q and -q
  as different rotations.
* quaternion_axis_between_EXP and quaternion_cross_product_EXP are not the
  operations their names describe.

Documentation and tests:

* Doxygen documents the functions from the implementation.
* The README has a coding standard and the numerical principles.
* Tests for the matrix4 multiply properties, quaternion_inverse with unit
  and non-unit quaternions, and the slerp shortest arc.
* A test that the matrix4 and quaternion rotations agree.
* CI builds with HYP_NO_RANDOM.
